Description: obs-websocket: a hotkey triggered by name runs on the UI thread
 TriggerHotkeyByName called the hotkey's callback on obs-websocket's own request thread (a Qt thread pool's), while a
 key press reaches the same callback on the UI thread through the frontend's router (OBSBasic::HotkeyTriggered queues
 it to OBSBasic::ProcessHotkey). The frontend's callbacks show and hide widgets: OBSBasic.EnablePreview and
 DisablePreview call EnablePreviewDisplay, which sets the preview's visibility, and Qt allows that only on the main
 thread ("QWidget and all its subclasses, are not reentrant. They can only be used from the main thread", Qt 6,
 Threads and QObjects). Measured on OBS 33.0.1 with the preview a declared 3D area: at the first hide the request thread
 made six QObjects whose parent lives on the main thread ("QObject::setParent: Cannot set parent, new parent is in a
 different thread"), and under load OBS died at a show ("malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk detected", "double free or
 corruption (!prev)").
 The task is queued inside the UI thread, as obs-websocket's own UI requests queue theirs (SetStudioModeEnabled), and
 waited for unless the request runs on the graphics thread (a SerialFrame batch), which the UI thread may itself be
 waiting for; the hotkey's id is passed by value. TriggerHotkeyByKeySequence already takes the router, through
 obs_hotkey_inject_event().
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 61, milestone 3, continuation 6)
Forwarded: no, OBS asks for human-written submissions only (CONTRIBUTING.md, AI/Machine Learning Policy)
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
diff --git a/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_General.cpp b/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_General.cpp
index 0bd5436..46b9086 100644
--- a/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_General.cpp
+++ b/obs-websocket-5-7-6/src/requesthandler/RequestHandler_General.cpp
@@ -265,8 +265,18 @@ RequestResult RequestHandler::TriggerHotkeyByName(const Request &request)
 	if (!hotkey)
 		return RequestResult::Error(RequestStatus::ResourceNotFound, "No hotkeys were found by that name.");
 
-	obs_hotkey_trigger_routed_callback(obs_hotkey_get_id(hotkey), true);
-	obs_hotkey_trigger_routed_callback(obs_hotkey_get_id(hotkey), false);
+	// A key press reaches a hotkey's callback on the UI thread, through the frontend's router, and the frontend's
+	// callbacks show and hide widgets (OBSBasic.EnablePreview), which Qt allows only on that thread. Queue the task
+	// inside of the UI thread to prevent race conditions, and wait for it unless this request runs on the graphics
+	// thread (a SerialFrame batch), which the UI thread may itself be waiting for.
+	obs_queue_task(
+		OBS_TASK_UI,
+		[](void *param) {
+			auto id = (obs_hotkey_id)(uintptr_t)param;
+			obs_hotkey_trigger_routed_callback(id, true);
+			obs_hotkey_trigger_routed_callback(id, false);
+		},
+		(void *)(uintptr_t)obs_hotkey_get_id(hotkey), !obs_in_task_thread(OBS_TASK_GRAPHICS));
 
 	return RequestResult::Success();
 }
